john.grundy@monash.edu (J. Grundy), omar.haggag@monash.edu (O. Haggag).significantly [ 6]. Traditional software components are deterministic
and developed through a deductive development process by explicitly
coding the system’s required behavior. In contrast, ML component
development follows an inductive process by exploring data and rec-
ognizing patterns [ 7]. ML components are dynamic and it is extremely
difficult to specify their ‘well-defined’ behavior [ 6,8]. Unlike software
engineers, ML engineers need to perform exploratory steps to identify
and curate datasets, select relevant features, select the most suitable ML
model, tune hyperparameters, monitor the ML component, and re-train
